headers {
  User-Agent: LiveOL Bruno
  Accept-Encoding: gzip, br
}

docs {
  # LiveOL - Liveresultat

  Two folders over the same competition, so the new REST API and the legacy
  `api.php` endpoints can be compared request for request:

  - **new-api/**    `https://api.orienteering.services`
  - **legacy-api/** `https://liveresultat.orientering.se/api.php`
  - **quirks/**     the behaviours the migration plan depends on, each clickable

  Matching pairs (same `seq` in both folders):

  | seq | legacy | new |
  | --- | --- | --- |
  | 1 | `getcompetitions` | `GET /competitions` |
  | 2 | `getcompetitioninfo` | `GET /competitions/{id}` |
  | 3 | `getclasses` | `GET /competitions/{id}/classes` |
  | 4 | `getclassresults` | `GET /competitions/{id}/classresults?class=` |
  | 5 | `getclubresults` | `GET /competitions/{id}/clubresults?club=` |
  | 6 | `getlastpassings` | `GET /competitions/{id}/passings` |
  | - | none | `GET /competitions/{id}/remaining` |
  | - | none | `GET /competitions/{id}/export` |

  ## Things to look at when comparing

  - **Change detection.** Legacy uses `last_hash` in the query and answers
    `status: "NOT MODIFIED"`. The new API uses `ETag` / `If-None-Match` and answers
    **304**. Run "Class results", then "Class results (conditional)".
  - **Casing.** `splitcontrols` became `splitControls`.
  - **Class list.** `[{ className }]` became a plain `string[]`.
  - **New result flag.** `DT_RowClass: "new_result"` is gone; rows carry `changed`
    and `startChanged` as UNIX seconds instead.
  - **Formatting.** Legacy needs `unformattedTimes=true` for integers, and
    `getclubresults` has no such switch, so it returns `"19:03"` / `"+02:51"`.
    The new API always returns hundredths of a second as integers.
  - **`/export` is not a superset.** It has runner ids that `classresults` lacks,
    but no `place`, `timeplus` or `progress`.

  The write endpoints (`POST /competitions`, `PUT /competitions/{id}`, `/mop`,
  `/upload`) are deliberately absent: they create or mutate real competitions on a
  live shared service, and LiveOL is a read-only consumer.

  Base URLs and the competition under test live in `environments/production.bru`.
}
